Z||000000||84 2in1||06-15-2001||07:30 PM||||still looking at adding a turbo on my 2.5. found a complete turbo uint on a Nissan Pulsar NX for very cheap. Aftr i get the uint Where do I start instaling this thing?-B-||||reg||12
Z||000001||erikred||06-15-2001||10:01 PM||||You may want to start by changing to stronger rods and pistons. If you just want some extra HP and do not want to screw with taking the motor apart, get a boost controled timming retard (Crane or MSD). Then cut off the bottom of the exhaust manifold and weld an adapter flange to it. Make sure to mount the turbo to the engine (homade brackets) otherwise the manifold will crack. Next fabricate a air box to go on the TBI and plumb in the tubing to it. You can use some exhaust pipe and some no hub bands from the hardware store for this. On the intake side you could use some PVC attached to a K&N filter. You will probably also need to increase the fuel pressure under boost to compensate for the boost pressure. Maybe you could use a Kenne Belle Boost-a-pump. Finally remember to start with the boost set low and use premium  fuel. This is basically what some one else has already done. He used to have a site, but it is no longer on the web. He said the motor did ok and he got over 200 HP. Be careful using the stock lower end though.<P>Let me know how it goes. I am planning on doing this to my 88 with a Chevy 2.0 turbo charger. I plan on using some beefier parts in the lower end though and I will not be able to do it until the funds allow. <BR>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Coupe'N||06-15-2001||10:32 PM||||Hey people, I have actually always thought about using the turbo off the Chrysler Laser/Dodge Daytona 2.2. I had a 86' laser before my fiero, dialed the boost up to 11 psi. I blew the engine shortly after because of no intercooler, too much boost, and no knowledge of ANYTHING!!!! haha. Well, now knowing a lil bit more, I would love to turbo my 87 coupe! I know the bottom end is the weak link in the duke engines, and you can get a nice cam/lifter set for the application needed. Its a big investment I would think though. <BR>Well, I just wanted to throw my $.02.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||10
Z||000003||84 2in1||06-15-2001||10:38 PM||||What caught my eye about this turbo setup it that it is a pretty small unit. Should not produce too much boost but spool up nicely. O2 sensor is after the turbo unit. Need to research this more. Do you happen to have this person's E-mail? May very well be a good resorce for info on this mod. Thanx for the reply-B-||||reg||6
